Fixed in commit 60146c31 ("Fixes #1166"). The retired github provider no longer appears in any list a user picks from. Build, test (all 42 test binaries), clippy with -D warnings, and fmt all pass.

The fix: I moved github out of KNOWN_PROVIDERS and into a new RETIRED_PROVIDERS table that pairs the name with its retirement message. Every place that shows KNOWN_PROVIDERS now leaves it out: the unknown-provider error, the /provider "available:" list, /provider completion, and the REPL's unknown-provider message. The new tests loop over both lists rather than typing provider names by hand.

What each `github` entry from #1166 became:
• API key lookup (`GITHUB_TOKEN`): removed. With a base URL, the request goes to the user's own server, not GitHub. Sending an ambient GITHUB_TOKEN there leaks a credential to the wrong host. A recording stub confirmed the token alone now sends nothing, and with API_KEY set the stub saw only that key.
• Default model, known-model list and the no-preset exemption: removed. --provider github --base-url X now needs --model, the same rule as custom.
• `MULTI_VENDOR_PROVIDERS` in `cli.rs`: removed. That entry could never be reached.
• `model_limits_note.rs`: both test-register rows removed. The production check still accepts retired names, so a base-URL run still gets the "guessed limits" warning (new test).
• The `github` branch in `agent_builder.rs`: kept, because the base-URL path runs through it. The built binary confirmed this.

Checks with the built binary:

| Command | Result |
|---|---|
| --provider nosuch | list no longer names github; exit 2 |
| --provider github (no base URL) | retirement message; exit 2 |
| --provider github --base-url … (no model) | "needs a model name"; exit 2 |
| same, plus --model foo | limits warning, then connection refused at the URL; exit 1 |

Decisions for you:
• Five files instead of the planned three. I added a one-line change in commands.rs. Without it, /provider github would have said "unknown provider", dropping the retirement message, and would have refused even with a base URL set, which breaks the behaviour 60546025 pinned. The other extra file is providers_key_tests.rs, which is the test module for providers.rs. I also corrected one outdated claim in ARCHITECTURE.md.
• Behaviour change: running github with a base URL now requires --model and no longer picks up GITHUB_TOKEN.

Not changed: in the REPL, /provider github with a base URL set now picks the generic default model (claude-opus-5-5) instead of openai/gpt-4o. /provider custom already does the same, so it isn't specific to this ticket.

No user-facing "see #1166" pointers exist in src or docs, so nothing breaks when the ticket closes.
